From ef40ff84150883becd1b9cbb55fc4e9f50deb6d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joe Hattori <hattorij@google.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:44:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover outlives relations between closure signature regions

hax::closure_sig replaces the regions that rustc erased from a closure signature with fresh, unrelated bound regions. A closure such as |a: &A| a.pools() then gets the signature fn(&'0 A) -> &'1 [T] without '0: '1, which its own body does not satisfy, and Aeneas fails with "Can't end abstraction ... non-endable".

Override the mir_borrowck query to read the region inference context of every closure nested in the checked item (rustc_borrowck::consumers), and record which signature regions the body requires to outlive which. Borrowck runs before later MIR passes steal the promoted MIR. When translating the generics of a closure item, add the recorded relations as region outlives predicates. Nothing is recorded with --skip-borrowck or for built MIR.
---
